## Control {{controlId}}: Identify Information System Users, Processes Acting on Behalf of Users, and Devices

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization identifies and authenticates all users, processes, and devices accessing CUI within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Microsoft Entra ID, multi-factor authentication, and device registration managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if mfaEnabled}}
**User Authentication:**
Microsoft Entra ID serves as the authoritative identity provider with {{authMethodsCount}} authentication methods configured:
{{#if authMethods}}
{{#each authMethods}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}})
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

All users authenticate via multi-factor authentication before accessing CUI resources, combining something they know (password) with something they have (authenticator app, FIDO2 key) or something they are (biometric).
{{else}}
Multi-factor authentication has not been confirmed. User identification relies on single-factor authentication only.
{{/if}}

{{#if userCount}}
**User Population:**
{{userCount}} users are managed in the tenant directory. The most recently active users include:
{{#if users}}
{{#each users}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{userPrincipalName}}) — {{#if accountEnabled}}Active{{else}}Disabled{{/if}} — Last sign-in: {{lastSignIn}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Process and Device Identification:**
{{caPoliciesTotalCount}} Conditional Access policies enforce device compliance and application identification requirements, ensuring only registered devices and authorized applications access CUI:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}})
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Entra ID authentication method configurations, user directory, Conditional Access policies, and device registration records.

